# AI Tutor engine.
#
# Nova answers with a real model when a provider key is present, and with the
# offline engine (your own documents + deterministic helpers) when it is not.
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in ONE option below; the backend loads it on
# startup. Never commit `.env` and never put a key in the frontend.
#
# Option 1 — a hosted provider (detected from its standard key):
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=...
# OPENAI_API_KEY=...
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=...
# GROQ_API_KEY=...
#
# Option 2 — explicit settings (win over the standard keys):
# STUDYHUB_AI_PROVIDER=openai          # openai | deepseek | openrouter | groq | mistral | together | xai | ollama | lmstudio | custom
# STUDYHUB_AI_API_KEY=...
# STUDYHUB_AI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# STUDYHUB_AI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
#
# Option 3 — a local runtime such as Ollama needs no key:
# STUDYHUB_AI_PROVIDER=ollama
# STUDYHUB_AI_MODEL=llama3.1

